<figure class="dgm bf16" aria-label="BF16 example: sign, exponent, and fraction">
  <div class="bit-strip">
    <div class="sign"><span>sign · 1 bit</span><b>0</b><small>positive</small></div>
    <div class="exponent"><span>exponent · 8 bits</span><b>01111111</b><small>127 − 127 = 0</small></div>
    <div class="fraction"><span>fraction · 7 bits</span><b>1010111</b><small>87 / 128</small></div>
  </div>
  <p class="value">(1 + 87/128) × 2⁰ = <strong>1.6796875</strong></p>
  <figcaption>Normal BF16 · 16 stored bits, highest bit first. The leading 1 is implicit.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
